Psalm 23 The Lord, Shepherd and Host - A psalm of David. I - The LORD is my shepherd; there is nothing I lack. In green pastures he makes me lie down; to still waters he leads me;

In green pastures he makes me lie down; to still waters he leads me; he restores my soul. He guides me along right paths for the sake of his name.

You set a table before me in front of my enemies; You anoint my head with oil; my cup overflows. Indeed, goodness and mercy will pursue me all the days of my life; I will dwell in the house of the LORD for endless days.

Daughters of kings are your lovely wives; a princess arrayed in Ophir’s gold comes to stand at your right hand. Forget your people and your father’s house,

honor him, daughter of Tyre. Then the richest of the people will seek your favor with gifts. All glorious is the king’s daughter as she enters, her raiment threaded with gold;

The maids of her train are presented to the king. They are led in with glad and joyous acclaim; they enter the palace of the king.

Daughters of kings are your lovely wives; a princess arrayed in Ophir’s gold comes to stand at your right hand. Forget your people and your father’s house,

honor him, daughter of Tyre. Then the richest of the people will seek your favor with gifts. All glorious is the king’s daughter as she enters, her raiment threaded with gold;

The maids of her train are presented to the king. They are led in with glad and joyous acclaim; they enter the palace of the king.

From ivory-paneled palaces stringed instruments bring you joy. Daughters of kings are your lovely wives; a princess arrayed in Ophir’s gold comes to stand at your right hand.

Forget your people and your father’s house, that the king might desire your beauty. He is your lord; All glorious is the king’s daughter as she enters, her raiment threaded with gold;

The maids of her train are presented to the king. The throne of your fathers your sons will have; you shall make them princes through all the land.

I - God is our refuge and our strength, an ever-present help in distress. Thus we do not fear, though earth be shaken and mountains quake to the depths of the sea,

Streams of the river gladden the city of God, the holy dwelling of the Most High. God is in its midst; it shall not be shaken; God will help it at break of day.

Selah Come and see the works of the LORD, who has done fearsome deeds on earth;

Psalm 5 Prayer for Divine Help - For the leader; with wind instruments. A psalm of David. I - Give ear to my words, O LORD; understand my sighing.

in the morning you will hear my voice; in the morning I will plead before you and wait. You are not a god who delights in evil; no wicked person finds refuge with you;

the arrogant cannot stand before your eyes. You hate all who do evil; You will protect them and those will rejoice in you who love your name.

Psalm 5 Prayer for Divine Help - For the leader; with wind instruments. A psalm of David. in the morning you will hear my voice; in the morning I will plead before you and wait.

You are not a god who delights in evil; no wicked person finds refuge with you; the arrogant cannot stand before your eyes. You hate all who do evil;

Drive them out for their many sins; for they have rebelled against you.

in the morning you will hear my voice; in the morning I will plead before you and wait. You are not a god who delights in evil; no wicked person finds refuge with you;

You are not a god who delights in evil; no wicked person finds refuge with you; the arrogant cannot stand before your eyes. You hate all who do evil;

you destroy those who speak falsely. A bloody and fraudulent man the LORD abhors.

May they be blotted from the book of life; not registered among the just! V - But here I am miserable and in pain; let your saving help protect me, God,

That will please the LORD more than oxen, more than bulls with horns and hooves: “See, you lowly ones, and be glad; you who seek God, take heart!

Let the heaven and the earth praise him, the seas and whatever moves in them!” They will dwell there and possess it;

May they be blotted from the book of life; not registered among the just! That will please the LORD more than oxen, more than bulls with horns and hooves:

“See, you lowly ones, and be glad; you who seek God, take heart! For the LORD hears the poor, and does not spurn those in bondage.

Let the heaven and the earth praise him, the seas and whatever moves in them!” They will dwell there and possess it;

Psalm 86 Prayer in Time of Distress - A prayer of David. I - Incline your ear, LORD, and answer me, for I am poor and oppressed. You are my God;

be gracious to me, Lord; to you I call all the day. Gladden the soul of your servant; to you, Lord, I lift up my soul.

Lord, you are good and forgiving, most merciful to all who call on you. LORD, hear my prayer; listen to my cry for help.

Psalm 86 Prayer in Time of Distress - A prayer of David. I - Incline your ear, LORD, and answer me, for I am poor and oppressed. You are my God;

You are my God; be gracious to me, Lord; to you I call all the day. Gladden the soul of your servant; to you, Lord, I lift up my soul.

Lord, you are good and forgiving, most merciful to all who call on you. LORD, hear my prayer; listen to my cry for help.

Psalm 87 Zion the True Birthplace - A psalm of the Korahites. A song. I - His foundation is on holy mountains, The LORD loves the gates of Zion more than any dwelling in Jacob. Glorious things are said of you, O city of God! Selah

See, Philistia and Tyre, with Ethiopia, “This one was born there.” And of Zion it will be said: “Each one was born in it.” The Most High will establish it;

the LORD notes in the register of the peoples: “This one was born there.” Selah So singers and dancers: “All my springs are in you.”

Give to the LORD, you families of nations, give to the LORD glory and might; give to the LORD the glory due his name! Bring gifts and enter his courts;

bow down to the LORD, splendid in holiness. Tremble before him, all the earth; declare among the nations: The LORD is king. The world will surely stand fast, never to be shaken. He rules the peoples with fairness.

declare among the nations: The LORD is king. The world will surely stand fast, never to be shaken. He rules the peoples with fairness. Let the heavens be glad and the earth rejoice; let the sea and what fills it resound; let the plains be joyful and all that is in them. Then let all the trees of the forest rejoice
